WEBVTT

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.900
He's a friend of mine. Have you seen him?

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.100
I know he came to this area, but...

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.900
He stayed the night here.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.880
Can't really tell you where
he went afterwards though.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.750
I see. Where in the world did he go?

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.590
Ah, sir.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.340
Huh?

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.210
It's getting dark.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.800
It's dangerous around these parts,
so why not stay the night?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:39.250
I got no other guests. 
I'll give you a big room.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.490
You're right. I'll take you up on that.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.050
Hm?

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:22.930
Huh?

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.570
What was that?

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.100
Huh?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:34.000
<i>The monochromatic empty eyes</i>
<i>of</i> <i>sapiens</i> <i>floating</i> <i>within the unreality</i>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.380
<i>Completely peerless flowing</i> <i>blood,</i>
<i>controlled</i> <i>and digitized</i>

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.050
<i>Just dark world (BOOM)</i>

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.470
<i>Glitter world (NO DOUBT)</i>

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.640
<i>Can you see?</i>

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.810
<i>(BOOING BOOING) Hellacious</i>

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.180
<i>Just dark world (BOOM)</i>

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.850
<i>Glitter world (NO DOUBT)</i>

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:49.890
<i>I can see!</i>

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.900
<i>The timing of the programming</i>

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.770
<i>Yea, gotcha!</i>

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:56.480
<i>I want to be eroded away (brain wash)</i>

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.650
<i>Up the blast! </i>

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:02.700
<i>Ah, this dying world </i>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:09.200
<i>Run like you're piercing through it</i>

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:15.540
<i>The rising flames burn everything away </i>

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.220
<i>Your resolve and your love</i>

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.800
<i>From darkness to the light</i>

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.690
There are places like this in the world.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.440
We've gone pretty far west, right?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.390
This area has been abandoned.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.640
Abandoned?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.900
Aggressive land development
and overproduction of chemical plants

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.980
devastated the surrounding environment.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.690
People living here started
leaving in great numbers.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.570
Abandoned by the government,
the town continues to deteriorate.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.680
The hearts of people with no
other place to go continue to darken.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.790
Can't something be done?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.750
We can only eliminate Horrors.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.710
We can't save the hearts of man.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.960
That may be true, but...

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.940
300 miles until the next town, huh?

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.240
Looks like we're camping tonight, too!

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.740
What?! This'll be the third day in a row!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.780
Can't be helped.
There aren't any places to stay.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.830
At least the two of you
are sleeping in the car, right?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.750
I've been in a sleeping bag
the past three days.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.460
My back is killing me!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.620
Who cares about you, Sword?!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.130
If you keep acting like a spoiled brat,

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:25.510
I'll take the car with Gina and
make you sleep in the sleeping bag!

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.380
That's fine.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.470
What? Really?!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.840
That will never happen.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.550
As expected.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.520
Isn't there one around here somewhere?

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.320
There <i>is</i> one!

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.410
Look! Over there!

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.450
There's something far down that way!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.660
Hello!

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.080
Do you have some vacant rooms?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.340
Welcome.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.040
Here's the key to room number 1.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:02.880
Thanks!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.210
Sophie.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:06.970
Thank you.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.760
Please come to the front desk
if you need anything.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.010
My name is Matthew.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.890
Why is there a motel here?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.330
Sword!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.440
They had a room vacant!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.270
Okay.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.610
Yes! I can take a shower!
I can sleep in a bed!

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.200
You can sleep in the sleeping bag, Sword!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.320
Gina and I will take the bed!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.500
Who was that?

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.840
Yay! A bed!

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:47.760
A sofa!

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.010
A fridge!

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:49.760
Hiya!

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.520
It's like I'm in heaven!

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.600
So sleepy.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.770
Yes.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.650
I never expected to find a place
to stay in an area like this.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.490
My back can't take this anymore.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.950
Gina, grab something for me.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.120
Me, too!

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.670
Get them yourself.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.200
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.290
Hey, Gina!

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.960
Which bed do you want, Gina?

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.510
I don't care.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:31.840
Really?! I wonder which I should take...

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.520
Huh?

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.210
What? He's already asleep?!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.850
Unbelievable!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.450
Are you the owner's kid?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:00.410
What's your name? We just got here today.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.500
Hand ball!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.470
It's all right, she just
went out to the front yard.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:20.810
How does a motel stay in
business in a place like this?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.290
I wonder if there's a reason for it.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.860
Well, let's keep an eye on things for now.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.750
As expected.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.290
I see. We're the same age!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.420
Are the two people with
you your brother and sister?

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.720
Oh, those two? They're my friends.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.550
Huh?

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.850
We're traveling together from Russell City.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.350
Russell City?

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.180
I lived in Russell City until I came here!

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.440
Really?!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.250
Then, do you know the
hotdog stand on 3rd street?!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.570
It's really good!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:10.820
I do!

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.780
Dad used to take me there a lot.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.780
Um, so why did you two move out here?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:23.310
My dad's company went
bankrupt and we couldn't stay.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.000
I see...

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.450
Dad has changed since we came here.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.420
He started to worry
about money all the time...

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:38.500
But I'm happy as long as my mom,
my dad, and I are together.

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:40.550
Yeah.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.770
Sorry for bringing this up.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.520
I just don't really have anyone to talk to.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.440
I know how you feel.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.060
Huh?

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.900
I have a big brother, but he went missing.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.410
All I want is to live together
with my brother.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.000
I'm sure your feelings
will get through to him!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.290
This brings me back to life!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.350
Where are all of you going from here?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.100
U-Um...

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.600
We're going west.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.570
Could it be, you're going to El Dorado?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.010
Do you know about El Dorado?

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:43.450
There are a lot of guests
going to El Dorado, lately.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.870
It seems you can find happiness there.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.630
No, we don't really
know the details ourselves.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.560
We've heard a lot of rumors,
so we got curious.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.920
I see.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:03.550
Either way, the increase
in customers are a great help.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.620
Not enough. Not enough at all.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:36.750
For the city. For the family.
We need money. Money.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:49.350
Shit. They're all making
fun of me... Money. Money!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.610
Darling, are you still at it?

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.440
Why don't you go to bed?

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.760
Darling.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.290
I saw the money in the safe.
Where did it come from?

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.160
Don't worry about it.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.670
Where did the guests
who've come previously go?

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.710
I told you, they left early.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.460
You've changed since we moved here!

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:21.010
You're so distant with George and me!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.430
What are you trying to say?

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.430
You're not trying to do
anything dangerous, are you?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.600
Don't say stupid things!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.430
Matthew!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.730
We only want the three
of us to live together happily!

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.710
Enough! I'm sick of this worthless subject!

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.110
Worthless subject?!

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.070
Matthew!

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.690
Are you going to do something to that girl

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.230
who's the same age as George?!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:45.950
Give it a rest! I'm doing 
this for your sakes!

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.120
Who ever wished for something like that?

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.580
Don't use us as an excuse.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.960
You wench! Is that all you can say?!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.540
--Are you making a fool of me, too?!
--Matthew, stop!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.840
I'll never forget what happened
when the company went under!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.470
I'm not going to end
my days in a place like this!

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.740
Stop!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.410
Stop. Please, stop...

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:21.360
I'm going back to the city.
I can't stay here. I can't.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.730
I'm going to sleep next to Gina.

00:13:29.730 --> 00:13:33.000
No! You're just planning
on staring at her chest.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.290
You know, I've been thinking.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.460
Aren't you misunderstanding something?

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:40.670
What do you mean?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:46.340
Listen, boobs are much
more sacred than you imagine.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:51.100
You and I wouldn't exist
in this world without boobs.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:56.350
Boobs are the source of life
and the mother of everything.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.270
It's obvious by looking at
the art left by ancient civilizations,

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:05.360
but boobs have always been
known as the symbol of fertility.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.870
In terms of motherhood, 
fortune, and health...

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:14.830
Boobs have been the unmoving
pillar of our past and present.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.540
Boobs are the most
revered things in the world!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.260
No, the universe!

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.250
Creep.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.300
--In other words, boobs <i>are</i> the universe!
--Oh, Gina! Welcome back!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.800
Where did you go?

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.420
--A quick break.
--In every era, boobs are warm and soft,

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.300
--Hey, Gina. Let's leave this guy
--In every era, boobs are warm and soft,

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.180
--and take a bath together.
--bringing the hearts of mankind
to tranquility and peace.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.050
--Sure!
--bringing the hearts of mankind
to tranquility and peace.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.640
--All right!
--bringing the hearts of mankind
to tranquility and peace.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:34.600
Boobs.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:35.600
Pervert.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.310
Who are you calling a pervert?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:41.060
Like I said, boobs are a sacred thing.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:45.570
You and I wouldn't exist
in this world without boobs.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.570
Boobs are the source of life and--

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.390
Shit!

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.270
How was it?

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.770
Were you able to
become friends with that boy?

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.770
Huh? Oh, George!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.440
Oh, his name is George?

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.990
What?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.320
Did you fall for him?

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.530
--What are you saying?! It's not like that!
--Okay. Okay.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.040
I'm telling you, it's really not like that!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.170
Oh! Mia!

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.450
You little trickster!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:46.380
...boobs have always been
known as the symbol of fertility.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:49.300
Well, then! Do you have
a person you like, Gina?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.970
Well, I wonder.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.680
Huh? No fair!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.140
You like someone, don't you?!

00:15:55.140 --> 00:16:00.100
Well, I think you're still
too young for me to tell you.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.330
Sophie.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.300
What?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.150
Do you remember what
I told you on the way here?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:27.800
Yeah.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:33.310
We can only protect the lives
of people by eliminating Horrors.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.510
Even if doing so
leaves behind a harsh reality.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.960
It's impossible to remove all the pain.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.520
What do you mean?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:49.770
Get back!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.120
Hey! You guys okay?!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.250
Looks like a liquid-based Horror
is possessing this motel.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.920
I see.

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.440
You were pretty fast today.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:31.030
What's wrong?
Did the prey today taste bad?

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.740
It's you.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.780
I told you not to come to the basement.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:41.410
Wh-What is that?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.450
Ahh.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:47.920
This thing is something
that will bring me back glory.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.880
What are you talking about?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.270
I'll tell you.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:56.030
A little after we came here,

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:00.890
I happened to see this thing attack a guest.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:24.240
Even though I had planned
to run this motel here.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.370
Why do I have to deal with this?

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:29.270
I can't stay in business
with a motel that eats its guests.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.400
But, you know,

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.000
that's when I understood.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.590
This is a gift from god.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:42.550
My luck has finally turned around.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.390
I'll use this thing to
start over in Russell City.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.230
Matthew, you've gone crazy.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.270
Why don't you understand?!

00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:56.280
This is a once in a lifetime chance!

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.990
Then, tell me what you wish for.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:18:59.730
Huh?

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.890
What is your desire?

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.690
I will grant you what you wish.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:11.150
I can't stand living
pathetically like this any longer.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:14.360
I don't want to stay here with nothing,
in the middle of nowhere,

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.590
until I die!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.550
--Grant me my wish!
--Matthew...

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:24.850
I'm definitely going to succeed
once again in Russell City!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:32.520
No! Matthew! No!

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:36.860
No! Matthew! No! Save me!

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.320
No! No! No!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.950
No!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.750
Leave it to us.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:07.160
What is that? What's happening?

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.040
Stay still.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.810
Don't get close!

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.440
George! Where is George?!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:22.490
Mom?!

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.070
Get in!

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.780
Fade away into the darkness!

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.330
Matthew.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.310
Matthew.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.020
I rewrote their memories.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.800
The motel was hit by
a tornado and Matthew died.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.080
Was there really nothing
we could do to save him?

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:51.910
Someone possessed
by a Horror will never return to normal.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.870
They will only continue
attacking and eating humans.

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.290
Let's go.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:21:59.820
Yeah...

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.180
Let's go.

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:41.670
<i>When I close my eyes I feel</i>
